From: nixos-m4pro
Subject: [PATCH] apple: rtkit_helper: take the stream from a multi-cell iommus

The J614s device tree of this repository describes the MTP DART with
Asahi's five-cell specifier (stream, then the DMA window), so the helper
found no DART, could not keep its bypass ("J614s: MTP DART bypass
unavailable (-19)") and the internal keyboard never started. The stream
is the first cell either way.
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-apple/rtkit_helper.c	2026-11-14 13:05:15.151459700 +0530
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-apple/rtkit_helper.c	2026-11-14 13:05:15.165004576 +0530
@@ -100,8 +100,11 @@
 		priv->dma_end = range[0] + range[1];
 	}
 
-	/* A live handoff additionally needs the DART left in bypass. */
-	if (args.args_count == 1 &&
+	/*
+	 * A live handoff additionally needs the DART left in bypass. The first
+	 * cell is the stream; Asahi-style trees add a DMA window after it.
+	 */
+	if (args.args_count >= 1 &&
 	    !uclass_get_device_by_ofnode(UCLASS_IOMMU, args.node, &priv->dart))
 		priv->dart_sid = args.args[0];
 }
